_🎯 Functional Correctness_ | _🟡 Minor_ | _⚡ Quick win_

**Warn before saving a side row whose App family matches the other Debate side.**

`staged` checks a change with `app::row_in`. The same-family rule is not in `row_in`. It is only in `debate_inputs` (src/orchestrator/app.rs Lines 216-222). The trigger is simple: with the default `side_a` on claude, pick `claude` for `side_b`, then pick `default`. `/config` saves the pair and shows a green "saved" note. During a live run, the next Debate then stops with "side_a and side_b both run Anthropic models: the Debate needs two families".

A hard refusal is wrong here. You can edit only one row at a time, so swapping the two sides always passes through a same-family state. Keep the save. When `key` is `side_a` or `side_b`, compare `row.app.family` with the other side's family in the staged doc. If they match, set a warning note.

<details>
<summary>♻️ Sketch</summary>

```rust
// in save(), after the write succeeds
let key = ROWS[row].key;
if let Some(other) = match key { "side_a" => Some("side_b"), "side_b" => Some("side_a"), _ => None } {
    let same = app::row_in(&doc, other, Path::new(""))
        .ok()
        .zip(app::app(&value(&doc, row, Field::App)))
        .is_some_and(|(o, a)| o.app.family == a.family);
    if same {
        st.note = Some((format!("saved: {name} {new}. Both Debate sides now run one family: the Debate will not start until one moves."), ORANGE));
    }
}
```
</details>

